{"id":"orationes.ave-maria","title":"Ave María","category":"orationes","section":"orationes-communes","variant":"devotional","sung":false,"st":"working-edition","ad":5,"adw":2,"about":{"pl":"Pierwsza część Pozdrowienia anielskiego łączy słowa Gabriela (Łk 1, 28) i Elżbiety (Łk 1, 42), a w żadnym z tych wersetów nie ma imion Maryja i Jezus, które dodaje modlitwa. Druga część, prośba skierowana do Maryi, pochodzi z XVI wieku.","en":"The first part of the Hail Mary joins Gabriel's words (Lk 1:28) to Elizabeth's (Lk 1:42), and neither verse carries the names Maria and Iesus that the prayer supplies. The second part, the petition addressed to Mary, is of the sixteenth century."},"ac":{"pl":[24],"en":[24]},"seg":[{"id":"s01","type":"verse","w":[{"i":"w001","f":"Ave","l":"aveo","m":167},{"i":"w002","f":"María","l":"Maria","p":",","m":61},{"i":"w003","f":"grátia","l":"gratia","m":30},{"i":"w004","f":"plena","l":"plenus","p":";","m":57,"h":"w002"},{"i":"w005","f":"Dóminus","l":"dominus","m":60},{"i":"w006","f":"tecum","l":"tu","p":":","m":131},{"i":"w007","f":"benedícta","l":"benedictus","m":25,"h":"w008"},{"i":"w008","f":"tu","l":"tu","m":143},{"i":"w009","f":"in","l":"in","m":0,"h":"w010"},{"i":"w010","f":"muliéribus","l":"mulier","p":",","m":40},{"i":"w011","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w012","f":"benedíctus","l":"benedictus","m":59,"h":"w013"},{"i":"w013","f":"fructus","l":"fructus","m":168},{"i":"w014","f":"ventris","l":"venter","m":69},{"i":"w015","f":"tui","l":"tuus","m":99,"h":"w014"},{"i":"w016","f":"Iesus","l":"Iesus","p":".","m":34}],"tr":{"pl":"Zdrowaś Maryjo, łaski pełna, Pan z Tobą, błogosławionaś Ty między niewiastami i błogosławiony owoc żywota Twojego, Jezus.","en":"Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee, blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus."},"g":{"pl":["zdrowaś","Maryjo","łaską","pełna","Pan","z Tobą","błogosławiona","Ty","między","niewiastami","i","błogosławiony","owoc","żywota","Twojego","Jezus"],"en":["hail","Mary","with grace","full","the Lord","with thee","blessed","thou","among","women","and","blessed","fruit","of the womb","thy","Jesus"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w001":"Pozdrowienie anioła w Łk 1, 28.","w003":"Ablativus zależny od „plena” (w004).","w004":"Zgadza się z „María” (w002) i łączy z „grátia” (w003).","w005":"Podmiot zdania z domyślnym „est”: Pan [jest] z Tobą.","w006":"Połączenie „te” i „cum”. Przy zaimkach osobowych „cum” stoi po zaimku.","w007":"„Benedícta [es] tu” — z domyślnym „es”.","w012":"Zgadza się z „fructus” (w013) i dlatego ma rodzaj męski.","w014":"Dopełniacz zależny od „fructus” (w013).","w015":"Zgadza się z „ventris” (w014).","w016":"Apozycja (dopowiedzenie) do „fructus” (w013): owoc… — Jezus."},"en":{"w001":"The angel's greeting in Lk 1:28.","w003":"Ablative complement of “plena” (w004).","w004":"Agrees with “María” (w002) and takes “grátia” (w003).","w005":"Subject with an understood “est”: the Lord [is] with thee.","w006":"A combination of “te” and “cum”. With personal pronouns, “cum” follows the pronoun.","w007":"“Benedícta [es] tu” — with “es” understood.","w012":"Masculine in agreement with “fructus” (w013).","w014":"A genitive dependent on “fructus” (w013).","w015":"Agrees with “ventris” (w014).","w016":"Apposition to “fructus” (w013): the fruit… — Iesus."}},"fc":{"pl":{"w001":[23]},"en":{"w001":[23]}}},{"id":"s02","type":"verse","speaker":"omnes","w":[{"i":"w017","f":"Sancta","l":"sanctus","m":57,"h":"w018"},{"i":"w018","f":"María","l":"Maria","p":",","m":61},{"i":"w019","f":"Mater","l":"mater","m":58},{"i":"w020","f":"Dei","l":"deus","p":",","m":54},{"i":"w021","f":"ora","l":"oro","m":41},{"i":"w022","f":"pro","l":"pro","m":0,"h":"w023"},{"i":"w023","f":"nobis","l":"nos","m":62},{"i":"w024","f":"peccatóribus","l":"peccator","p":",","m":169},{"i":"w025","f":"nunc","l":"nunc","m":32},{"i":"w026","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w027","f":"in","l":"in","m":0,"h":"w028"},{"i":"w028","f":"hora","l":"hora","m":30},{"i":"w029","f":"mortis","l":"mors","m":13},{"i":"w030","f":"nostræ","l":"noster","p":".","m":14,"h":"w029"},{"i":"w031","f":"Amen","l":"amen","p":".","m":46}],"tr":{"pl":"Święta Maryjo, Matko Boża, módl się za nami grzesznymi teraz i w godzinę śmierci naszej. Amen.","en":"Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen."},"g":{"pl":["Święta","Maryjo","Matko","Boga","módl się","za","nami","grzesznikami","teraz","i","w","godzinie","śmierci","naszej","amen"],"en":["Holy","Mary","Mother","of God","pray","for","us","sinners","now","and","at","the hour","of death","our","amen"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w017":"Zgadza się z „María” (w018).","w019":"Apozycja (dopowiedzenie) do „María” (w018).","w020":"Dopełniacz zależny od „Mater”: Matka Boga.","w023":"Ablativus po „pro” (w022).","w024":"Apozycja (dopowiedzenie) do „nobis” (w023).","w028":"Ablativus po „in” (w027) w określeniu czasu.","w029":"Dopełniacz zależny od „hora” (w028).","w030":"Zgadza się z „mortis” (w029)."},"en":{"w017":"Agrees with “María” (w018).","w019":"Apposition to “María” (w018).","w020":"Genitive dependent on “Mater”: Mother of God.","w023":"Ablative after “pro” (w022).","w024":"Apposition to “nobis” (w023).","w028":"Ablative after “in” (w027) in a temporal phrase.","w029":"Genitive dependent on “hora” (w028).","w030":"Agrees with “mortis” (w029)."}}}]}